  "id": "exact-replication",
  "term": "exact replication",
  "definition": "Exact replication means repeating a study or experiment in a way that reproduces the original procedures, data resources, and analysis steps as closely as possible so the same results can be checked. In this source, it refers to providing enough software, data, and protocol detail for all experiments and findings to be reproduced exactly.",
